title: "Monochromatic Sublattices in Random and Cardinality Colourings of the Boolean Lattice"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Bhattacharjee
    given-names: Deep
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0003-0466-750X"
    affiliation: "Formerly, Electro-Gravitational Space Propulsion Laboratory (EGSPL), Bhubaneswar, Odisha 751030, India"
    email: d.bhattacharjee@erl-forschung.de
version: 1.0.0
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/creelie/D7"
keywords:
  - Boolean lattice
  - sublattices
  - Ramsey theory
  - random colourings
  - Erdős problems
abstract: >-
  Let f(n) be the largest m such that every 2-colouring of the subsets of an n-element set has a
  monochromatic sublattice with m members. In a uniformly random k-colouring the largest
  monochromatic sublattice has (1+o(1)) n log_k n members with high probability, so
  f(n) <= (1+o(1)) n log_2 n. The value of f(n) is found for n <= 22 and n = 24.
